  "cause": "**The death toll in one Zaporizhzhia village passed forty, and the evidence of how it happened came from a camera on a policeman who died in it.** Ukraine's national police released **bodycam footage on Wednesday** that the **BBC** reports shows the interval between two Russian strikes on **Kamyshuvakha**: residents going down into an underground shelter after the first bomb, an official's voice on a two-way radio warning that more glide bombs were inbound, a police officer telling people *\"Quickly [go] to the shelter!\"*, and then a blast and flames as the shelter itself is hit, at which point the recording stops. **BBC Verify** confirmed the video was filmed at the same location as separate footage of the aftermath released by Ukraine's state emergencies service. **President Zelensky** said **nine aerial bombs** were dropped, some weighing **3,000kg**: *\"First, they hit people who came to receive humanitarian aid, and then rescuers and police officers who arrived at the scene.\"* He said **more than 30 people may still be under the rubble** and that the search was in its third day; **Al Jazeera** and **The Guardian** report the toll now confirmed at **40**. The shelter was at least two floors underground, beside a school being used to distribute aid. Zelensky added: *\"Unfortunately, there has been very little reaction from the world to this insane attack\"* — one of *\"thousands\"* of Russian war crimes. The Russian military has not publicly commented. **The village was hit twice, and the second strike was aimed at the response to the first.** This is the tactic the Ukrainians call a double-tap: a first strike that creates casualties and a crowd, and a second that arrives while police, medics and rescuers are working the rubble. The bodycam is unusual not because it shows a war crime but because it shows the interval — the thirty or forty seconds in which the warning arrived, the instruction was given, and the shelter was still hit. A shelter two floors down is not a place people can be moved out of quickly, and nine glide bombs do not require precision to find a village. **In Brussels and Abu Dhabi, the war was being scheduled while the rubble was still being searched.** Zelensky said he spoke *\"in great detail for an hour-and-a-half\"* with Trump's envoys **Steve Witkoff** and **Jared Kushner** ahead of **trilateral talks between Ukraine, Russia and the US on 10–11 November in Abu Dhabi** — the first since February, when the process was suspended. His team also met in **Brussels** with the **US, EU, France, Britain, Germany, NATO and the World Bank** on post-war reconstruction, with discussions on **security guarantees** continuing on Thursday. Analysts expect no major breakthrough. Since February, Moscow has stepped up attacks while Kyiv has virtually run out of Western-supplied interceptors — which is the condition under which a village gets nine glide bombs and no interceptor.",
